er assessment (technical), computer skills. Concerns: weak memory for numbers (attention/accuracy), nasty remarks (crew cooperation, professional communication). So mixed.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Strengths: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical competence. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Good.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: adaptability, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: know-it-all (cooperation), hot temper (stress resilience). Mixed.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely Candidate C has strong technical, decision, calmness, but communication issues and egocentric may be serious for crew cooperation. Candidate B has reliability and stress but nasty remarks severe. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but not open to new ideas and show-off. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Probably Candidate C's strengths align with many criteria: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence, attention? Not mentioned attention but quick decisions. However communication issues could be a big problem for cockpit. But maybe can be mitigated? Egocentric also concerning.\n\nCandidate B's conscientiousness and stress handling are good, but nasty remarks are severe for crew cooperation. That may outweigh.\n\nCandidate A's anticipation and leadership are valuable for long-distance, but not open to new ideas could affect adaptability. Show-off may affect crew.\n\nCandidate D's responsibility and problem solving are good, but hot temper is serious for stress.\n\nThus maybe Candidate C is best despite communication concerns, because technical and decision are critical. But we need to argue with evidence.\n\nWe'll state recommendation for Candidate C, citing quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical understanding, but note concerns about communication and egocentric, but overall strengths outweigh.\n\nLet's produce public message."}
